{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"26"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5502","displayName":"Radko Gudas","shortName":"R. Gudas"},"type":"hit-credited"},{"athlete":{"id":"3115033","displayName":"Ryan Donato","shortName":"R. Donato"},"type":"hitted"}]},{"id":"401892578000000070","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"On-Ice Official","type":{"id":"516","text":"Stoppage","abbreviation":"stoppage"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:30"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}},{"id":"401892578000000760","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Sam Reinhart faceoff won against Roman Kantserov","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:30"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"26"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3114722","displayName":"Sam Reinhart","shortName":"S. Reinhart"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"5149231","displayName":"Roman Kantserov","shortName":"R. Kantserov"}}]},{"id":"401892578000000950","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Giveaway by Artyom Levshunov","type":{"id":"1402","text":"Giveaway","abbreviation":"giveaway"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:58"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"4"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"5206648","displayName":"Artyom Levshunov","shortName":"A. Levshunov"},"type":"giver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1847","fullName":"United Center","address":{"city":"Chicago","state":"IL","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1847.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18117,"officials":[{"fullName":"David Brisebois","displayName":"David Brisebois","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jon McIsaac","displayName":"Jon McIsaac","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Chris Schlenker","displayName":"Chris Schlenker","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Onni Hautamaki","displayName":"Onni Hautamaki","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Lars Eller scores late goal as Panthers top Blackhawks 3-2","description":"— Lars Eller's first goal of the season, with 2:23 left in the third period, lifted the Florida Panthers to a 3-2 win over the Chicago Blackhawks on Sunday.","story":"CHICAGO -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3946/lars-eller\">Lars Eller</a>'s first goal of the season, with 2:23 left in the third period, lifted the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/fla/florida-panthers\">Florida Panthers</a> to a 3-2 win over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/chi/chicago-blackhawks\">Chicago Blackhawks</a> on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Eller beat <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565234/spencer-knight\">Spencer Knight</a> with a high shot just inside the left post as he raced down right wing and took advantage of Chicago line change. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024854/matthew-tkachuk\">Matthew Tkachuk</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5103599/sandis-vilmanis\">Sandis Vilmanis</a> also scored for Florida, which ended two-game losing streak.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149231/roman-kantserov\">Roman Kantserov</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080227/ryan-greene\">Ryan Greene</a> connected for Chicago, which has dropped three straight.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4587845/akira-schmid\">Akira Schmid</a> made 19 saves, while Knight stopped 29 shots.\n\n\r\n              The Blackhawks failed to score on seven power-play chances, including two brief 5-on-3 advantages, lowering their NHL-worst conversion rate to 8.33%. \n\n\r\n              Blackhawks defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565225/bowen-byram\">Bowen Byram</a> missed his fourth game with an upper-body injury. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080148/kevin-korchinski\">Kevin Korchinski</a>, Chicago’s top pick in the 2022 draft, seventh overall, filled in and played his second game this season.\n\n\r\n              Florida forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042088/carter-verhaeghe\">Carter Verhaeghe</a> played in his 500th NHL game and tallied an assist.\n\n\r\n              The Panthers outshot Chicago 15-6 in the first period and took a 2-1 lead.\n\n\r\n              Greene opened the scoring 2:34 in, getting just enough of a wobbling puck to direct it past Schmid after Korchinski’s shot from the point missed the net and bounced in front.\n\n\r\n              Vilmanis popped in a rebound of Sam Reinhart’s shot from a scramble to tie it at 6:49.\n\n\r\n              Tkachuk’s power-play goal, five seconds after <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042056/tyler-bertuzzi\">Tyler Bertuzzi</a> was sent off for tripping, gave Florida a 2-1 lead with 5:39 left in the first. Seth Jones’ shot from the point struck Tkachuk on the arm and bounded in.\n\n\r\n              Kantserov tied it at 2-2 at 11:15 of the second. He beat Schmid low on a screened shot from the right circle, capping a strong shift with linemates <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3735/patrick-kane\">Patrick Kane</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149125/connor-bedard\">Connor Bedard</a>.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Panthers: At Winnipeg on Tuesday in finale of four-game trip.\n\n\r\n              Blackhawks: Host Los Angeles on Tuesday to complete a seven-game homestand.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-25T22:08:46Z"}}